This project is the PiShock Discord Activity, a production-ready application designed to enable consensual control of PiShock electrical devices within a multiplayer Discord environment. It runs as a Discord Activity, allowing users to interact with PiShock devices directly from Discord voice channels or DMs.

Key functionalities include:

Sending shock, vibrate, and beep commands to PiShock devices.
Multiplayer support, enabling multiple users to participate with their own devices.
Real-time updates for participant lists and activity feeds.
Robust safety features such as user-configurable intensity/duration limits, explicit consent mechanisms, a ban system, and comprehensive activity logging for transparency and accountability.
Secure, encrypted storage for PiShock credentials.
The architecture involves:

A frontend built with React 18, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, and Vite, utilizing the Discord Embedded App SDK.
A serverless backend powered by Cloudflare Workers and Cloudflare KV for data storage (user data, activity logs, instance management).
Integration with the PiShock Legacy & V3 APIs for device control.
Deployment on Cloudflare Pages with Workers.
Critical Safety Warning: This application controls electrical shock devices that can cause physical harm, injury, or death if misused. All design and implementation decisions must prioritize user safety, consent, and legal compliance.

